Built-in sound bank `builtin:classic` (`classic.rkskin`, BLAKE3 495878159fc794af99b61b56ab6d35128f53ce199f6a30a15b2c24872768d32d): Xfire's "Classic sound pack".

Provenance
  Imported by `cargo xtask import-xfire-data` (plan E7.7.3) from the project owner's
  Xfire install tree, git commit ba066924 ("xfire re'd"; removed from the tree by
  5a20b508), restored into the git-ignored `legacy/unpacked/`:
    legacy/unpacked/sounds/classic.zip  BLAKE3 182140985b321b46c14a05b44f76fb4feb7e7811e3c00572fcbb736650af7c43

Licence
  This is Xfire, Inc. content; Xfire is defunct. The project owner ruled on 2026-10-15
  that Xfire's own assets may be used in Rekindle. Rekindle's MIT LICENSE does not cover
  it.

How it was made
  Each cue is the file `sounds.xml` names for its Xfire sound type, re-encoded to PCM16
  WAV by the skin validator. Xfire had no mention or busy sound: mention plays "Receive
  Message" (Xfire's sound for every incoming message) and busy plays "Call End". The
  package's one variant has an empty token file (the registry defaults).
    message <- recv.wav
    mention <- recv.wav
    sign-on <- online.wav
    sign-off <- offline.wav
    call <- ringing.wav
    ringback <- callerring.wav
    busy <- hangup.wav
  Xfire sound types with no Rekindle cue (not imported):
    In-game Receive Message (igrecv.wav)
    Send Message (send.wav)
    User Arrived (entroom.wav)
    User Left (leftroom.wav)
    Call Start (pickup.wav)
    Screenshot (screenshot.wav)
